  "above_fold_text": "Overview On demand 2026 recap keynote & launches Session Catalog Speakers Sponsors FAQs Notify me June (14) 15-16, 2027 New York, NY DASH 2027 is coming—Be in the know Sign up for exclusive previews and announcements. Join us in NYC, June (14) 15-16, 2027. Business Email* By submitting this form, you agree to the Privacy Policy and Cookie Policy and agree to sharing your information with Datadog. Sign me up!",
  "visible_text": "Skip to main content\nOVERVIEW\nON DEMAND\n2026 RECAP\nFAQS\nNOTIFY ME\n\nJUNE (14) 15-16, 2027\n\nNEW YORK, NY\n\nDASH 2027 is coming—Be in the know\n\nSign up for exclusive previews and announcements. Join us in NYC, June (14) 15-16, 2027.\n\nBusiness Email*\nBy submitting this form, you agree to the Privacy Policy and Cookie Policy and agree to sharing your information with Datadog.\nSIGN ME UP!\nThe DASH Experience\nDive into what’s next in AI\n\nBe the first to know about how Datadog is accelerating AI-powered observability and security.\n\nGo from hype to hands-on know-how\nLearn from the leaders, and the doers\nExpand your AI reach with partners\nYour 2026 DASH Recap\n\nWHAT'S NEW\n\nExplore the 2026 launches\n\nRELIVE DASH 2026\n\nWatch the sessions\n\nDASH 2026 AT A GLANCE\n4K+\nattendees\n20+\nworkshops\n60+\nsessions\n30+\nspeakers\n2026 Speakers\nAdam Scott\n\nACTOR\nGUEST SPEAKER\n\nOlivier Pomel\n\nCEO & CO-FOUNDER\nDATADOG\n\nAlexis Lê-Quôc\n\nCTO & CO-FOUNDER\nDATADOG\n\nYanbing Li\n\nCHIEF PRODUCT OFFICER\nDATADOG\n\nClément Delangue\n\nCEO & CO-FOUNDER\nHUGGING FACE\n\nThibault Sottiaux\n\nHEAD OF PRODUCT AND PLATFORM\nOPENAI\n\nZe Wang\n\nHEAD OF R&D DATA ENGINEERING\nSANOFI\n\nTom Occhino\n\nCHIEF PRODUCT OFFICER\nVERCEL\n\nSholto Douglas\n\nMEMBER OF TECHNICAL STAFF\nANTHROPIC\n\nDaksh Gupta\n\nCEO\nGREPTILE\n\nZach Lloyd\n\nCEO\nWARP\n\nJay V\n\nCEO\nOPENCODE\n\nSinthanai Natarajan\n\nSENIOR EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR\nJPMORGAN CHASE\n\nVIEW ALL SPEAKERS\nPrevious Item\nNext Item\n\nTHANKS TO OUR 2026 SPONSORS\n\nSEE ALL SPONSORS\nYOUR STORY STARTS HERE\n“One of the most valuable parts of DASH is having direct access to people who really know the platform and to other teams solving the same problems. It opens your eyes to capabilities you didn’t even realize you weren’t using.”\nJustin\n\nEngineering Leader, Large Technology Platform\n\n“Talking with other engineers about how they actually use Datadog has been one of the most valuable parts of being here.”\nRick\n\nBackend Engineer, Mobile Gaming\n\n“DASH creates a really welcoming environment to grow, connect with others, and gain a broader perspective on observability and AI that helps us evolve our infrastructure with confidence.”\nMercedes\n\nTechnical Program Manager, Healthcare Technology\n\n“We operate across AWS, Azure, on-prem, and microservices. Being at DASH helped me understand how to bring all of that into one view and use Datadog in the best way.”\nSuhail\n\nDevOps & Site Reliability Engineer, Financial Services\n\n“If you want to understand where observability is going—especially with AI—you need to be at DASH. This is where you see what’s next.”\nSimon\n\nSolutions Architect, Enterprise Software\n\n“DASH is the best way to understand where observability is going. You see what’s coming next and how the technology is being applied across industries.”\nTheresa\n\nDirector of Commercial Activities, Technology Services & Consulting\n\n“DASH surprised me. I came looking for security insights, but I gained perspective on software engineering, AI, and where the industry is headed. I will be back.”\nAlia\n\nInformation Security Analyst, Professional Sports & Media\n\n“DASH was a game changer for us. Seeing how Datadog is applying AI to incident management reinforced how we can scale reliability across our organization.”\nAshish\n\nDirector of Engineering, Aerospace & Transportation Technology\n\nPrevious Item\nNext Item\nCAN'T WAIT FOR DASH 2027?\n\nCheck out other Datadog events and webinars.\n\nEXPLORE EVENTS\nJUNE (14) 15–16, 2027\nNEW YORK CITY\nThe future of AI & observability starts here\nNOTIFY ME\nCODE OF CONDUCT\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS\nPRIVACY\nCONTACT\nYOUR PRIVACY CHOICES\n© Datadog 2026",
